00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:42.180
You obviously chose the right cast

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:49.000
How much was there riffing on the set or screwing around or did you allow that to go on?

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.320
Tim: Oh, fuck yeah, I mean the whole

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:57.240
First of all, I can't stop it. Um, Ryan does it non-stop

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:00.100
and T.J. is completely uncontrollable

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.400
T.J.: Professional
Tim: I mean, really

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:05.140
Tim: Even when I would get angry at him and tell him to quit fucking around he would still

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:08.040
still do it but everybody was great

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.760
I mean, we had a great set for a first-time director

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:13.920
It's gotta be one of the best experiences I could hope for

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.160
because we had no drama, no difficulty

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:18.560
the studio was behind this for all the decisions

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:20.760
They didn't question anything that we did

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.800
Uh, even though they probably should have

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.260
Morena: I think Tim was the biggest drama on set, right?

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.440
Tim: Yeah. I'm a bit of a prima donna

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.420
Tim: very needy
Morena: The stuff that comes out of your mouth

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:33.140
Tim: Ryan had to hug me at least twice a day

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:35.760
Ryan: Ugh, he's such a cry-baby, God!

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:39.580
He's such a pervert, too. Everything that he-

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.960
This guy cries if he sees unadulterated rage

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:46.740
Like, it's like it like gets him

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:52.880
Tim: It's true. Ryan did this scene where he comes in at a pivotal part of the movie that I won't tell you about

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:56.780
and he's just so fucking angry and Ryan's this thing, he's like:

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:59.960
"Dude, I got like two fucking takes in me for this because I'm [GRUNTS]"

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.780
But it was brilliant! And so I choked up a little bit

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:05.540
Ryan: I found him weeping in the corner afterwards
Tim: It was so good.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:09.020
Ryan: I was like [GRIMACES] like non of the funny-dramatic stuff does it

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:11.540
just the pure rage. You should direct the next Hulk

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:15.200
You'd just be crying like a baby the whole time behind the monitor

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.200
Tim: I cry for the emotional stuff

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.020
Ryan: Then direct an episode of Nancy Grace

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:22.540
Tim: and then he got really jealous
[CROWD LAUGHING]

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:27.880
Tim: And then Ryan gets really jealous because on the third act Morena did this amazing scene

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:31.080
and I teared up again and then he did his side of it

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.780
and I was like "yeah, that was alright"

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:35.220
He's like "Where's my tears?"

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:37.580
Ryan: No, no

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:43.940
Chris: Were there things that you felt like "oh well maybe this is one step too far or maybe this is one step too"?

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:45.460
Morena: Only everyday

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:47.240
Ryan: Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah
Morena: Every scene

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:49.600
Ryan: Yeah, there's stuff that I like would get home

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:52.500
I would be lying awake in bed and I would text Tim just to say:

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:56.560
"hey, that thing I said, that extra joke at the end of that scene when I'm walking out of the cab,

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:59.840
could you make sure that's never seen by anyone?"

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:01.040
[CROWD LAUGHING]

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.980
Ryan: Because there's a number of organizations that will find me

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.180
[CROWD LAUGHING]

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:11.680
Tim: There was a rewrite T.J. Miller got involved in one of the scenes

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:14.160
and he wrote some of the meanest jokes

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:20.980
That's where I really said "you know we can't do this 'cause this is funny as shit but it's fucking mean"

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:21.920
It's just mean

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.600
Gina: Thank you! thank you and when you're-
T.J.: I am not mean!

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:27.140
Gina: when you're on the opposite end of those jokes.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:32.220
You're laughing and crying and then you go home and you literally cry.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.420
[CROWD LAUGHING]

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:34.520
Thank you

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:41.100
T.J.: It's true. I saw-Ryan's very strong, I don't know if you know ladies but he has a very muscular body

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:44.640
He's a strong man. And he was really sweet because when Tim would cry

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:47.380
he'd hold him like the little true, big baby that he is

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:48.580
[CROWD LAUGHING]

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.720
He'd rock him back and forth until Tim [MAKES SLEEPING AND SNORING SOUNDS]

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:52.440
Ryan: Yeah

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.040
T.J.: Then we'd all put on the suit and fuck around

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.960
[CROWD LAUGHING]

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:02.180
Chris: So, what can you say about this version of Deadpool without-

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:03.800
Obviously without giving away too much

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:05.300
What can you say to people? What can they expect?

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:10.340
I mean, I know we got a glimpse of it before but what-

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:14.740
Ryan: Well, it's everything, you know, that we love about the comics, I mean it's-

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.680
We have a guy that obviously is gonna break the fourth wall

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.260
Ryan: You're obviously gonna see what
[CROWD CHEERING]

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:25.300
And this is just my opinion but I think the most faithful

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:30.340
adaptation of a supersuit from a comic to a movie I've ever seen

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.080
[CROWD CHEERING]

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:34.060
And that's [UNINTELLIGIBLE NAME] I gotta shout him out

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.320
Uh, we have the Merc with the Mouth

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:39.760
The mouth is not at any point in our film sewn shut

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:42.200
[CROWD CHEERING]

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.700
Chris: Was that a condition?
Ryan: Yeah

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.100
Chris: You're nor sewing this mouth shut

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:51.360
Ryan: It was the only thing-I wasn't even paid, they just promised me that on this movie.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.100
But um, and yeah, you have your Merc with the Mouth

00:15:54.100 --> 00:16:00.200
You have the guy that is uh, doing his best to annoy the living shit out of everyone around him 24/7

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:04.040
Tim: And, you know what? Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick, the writers too.

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:06.140
Where are they? They're somewhere.
[CROWD CHEERING]

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:13.700
They deserve a lot of credit because this script, barn on is the best script I've ever read

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.740
[CLEARS THROAT] I get choked up, It's so good.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.500
Ryan: See what I'm saying?
Chris: No! What?

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.760
Tim: It's beautiful
Ryan: are you okay?

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:29.260
Tim: I do, the script is great and they were tireless about with me trying to get this movie made with Ryan

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:34.420
We never let up with the studio, just constantly annoying them

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:39.160
With e-mails to please make this movie. Rhett and Paul were there beside me the whole time saying

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:43.180
This is the best script we've ever written and it needs to be done, so.

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:47.340
Chris: Tim, you know, I gotta say
[CROWD CLAPPING]

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:52.120
Chris: We've never met before this moment. I didn't know this but I just

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:57.480
I see this crusty exterior and a chewy center inside that I really enjoy about you

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.280
Tim: Hottest middle-age director working

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:03.500
Chris: No! But you have to know that it's just important for this people to know that this is

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.100
that important to you, you know? Like this is a very

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:08.660
This is a very special and important character to people and so

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.020
If you came out like "yeah we made this hot superhero movie"

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.200
people would be like "fuck that guy!" But you, you know, like

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.380
You're sensitive and you love it and it means something to you and we actually

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:19.500
have some footage to show you guys because

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:20.700
[CROWD CHEERING]

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:27.660
Because you're good and you sat through a lot of T.J. and I making horse puns and so

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:31.620
I appreciate that and so let's show some never-before-seen footage

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:35.520
Chris: Come on, you guys! Ladies and gentlemen

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.780
Tim Miller, Ryan Reynolds and the cast of Deadpool!

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:39.980
[CROWD CHEERING]

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:11.060
[CROWD CHANTING "ONE MORE TIME"]

